            <ArticleTitle>SUNCT syndrome. Statuslike pattern.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>622-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Four SUNCT patients with a clinical &quot;SUNCT status&quot; witnessed by the investigators are reported. Such an extreme aggregation of typical attacks lasting for the better part of the day, 1 to 3 days in a row has not previously been observed. Appropriate supplementary examinations ruled out an intracranial lesion in all four patients. Indeed, an observation period of more than 5 years speaks against a symptomatic etiology of SUNCT in these cases. Although rarely seen, clinical status may be a feature of the SUNCT syndrome.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
